# 10 — Array Tools

> **For the agent reading this:** Read `plans/08-semantics-and-entities` §7 first (entities, instances, how an instance is a group for holes, and `expandInstance`), then `plans/thinking-05-performance` (why many small shapes are slow: draw calls). Arrays were deferred on purpose in `05` §11 ("live arrays share their machinery with prefabs") and listed in `thinking-01-entities` (circle, grid, row, stacking, noise). This phase adds the **array**: one node that repeats entities along a layout, live. It adds:
> - **the array node** (`array_N`): made from an instance with the inspector's **Array** button, it places **items** (instances of one or more entities) on a **layout**: a path, a circle, a grid or a scatter;
> - **following an outline:** a path layout can follow another node (a room's wall top, a volume's top, a ramp, a line), so battlements stay on the keep when the keep is resized;
> - **noise and variety:** seeded position and turn jitter, and several entities with weights (a forest of three trees);
> - **instanced drawing:** each array is drawn with `InstancedMesh`es, a few draw calls for hundreds of items, plus a small stats readout to measure it.
>
> Export to engines and the evals of `thinking-04` come later; the rest of editor performance (merging static shapes) is its own phase (`thinking-05`). The work is split into small increments (§10). Each one ends with the human ↔ agent loop still working and a browser checklist for Orlando. Add this phase's terms to `GLOSSARY.md` (marked "from 10") as they land. Log progress in a §13 at the end of this file, as 09 did.

