## 9. MCP surface

| Tool | Change |
|---|---|
| `draw_shapes` | type `array`: `entity` (one) or `entities` (`[{ entity, weight? }]`), `layout` (`{ type: "path" \| "circle" \| "grid" \| "scatter", ... }` as in §3), `facing?`, `rotation?`, `jitter?`, `turnJitter?`, `seed?`, `skip?`, `name?`, `parent?`. Refused for an unknown entity, a following target that can't be followed, and in Edit entity mode. The result gives the ID, the item count and any dropped or unfit items. |
| `update_nodes` | for arrays: `entities`, `layout` (fields merge into the layout of the same `type`; a different `type` replaces it), `facing`, `rotation`, `jitter`, `turnJitter`, `seed`, `skip`, `name`, `parent`, `locked`, `hidden`. `layout: { along: null }` unlinks. |
| `detach_instances` | takes array IDs too (an array becomes a group of instances). Its description says so. |
| `move_nodes`, `rotate_nodes`, `mirror_nodes`, `remove_nodes`, `group_nodes`, `ungroup` | handle arrays (§4, §6). `move_nodes` with `copy` copies an array as a node. |
